cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Trained Eye, its code or its model, please cite it as below."
title: "Trained Eye: Teach Your Glasses to Notice Anything"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Sheikh
    given-names: Amaan
repository-code: "https://github.com/amaan784/trained-eye"
identifiers:
  - type: url
    value: "https://huggingface.co/amaan784/trained-eye"
    description: "The fine-tuned LoRA adapter for Muse Glimmer 30B, with its model card"
license: MIT
date-released: 2026-11-04
abstract: >-
  Look at something for a few seconds, say what to watch for, and your Meta glasses speak
  up when it happens. Trained Eye turns one sentence and a short look into a small model,
  fine-tuned from Meta's open-weights Muse Glimmer, that watches for it and tells you.
keywords:
  - smart glasses
  - vision language model
  - fine-tuning
  - LoRA
  - Muse Glimmer
